MCP Runtime CLI provides commands to manage the MCP platform including:
- Container registry
- Kubernetes cluster
- MCP server deployments
- Platform configuration

Usage:
  mcp-runtime [command]

Available Commands:
  access      Manage grants and agent sessions
  adapter     Run agent-side adapters that inject issued MCP governance headers
  agent       Manage team-owned governance agents
  auth        Log in to the platform API and manage saved credentials
  bootstrap   Bootstrap cluster prerequisites (on-prem focused)
  catalog     Search MCP Runtime catalogs
  cluster     Manage Kubernetes cluster
  completion  Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  help        Help about any command
  registry    Manage container registry
  sentinel    Operate the bundled mcp-sentinel stack (admin only)
  server      Manage MCP servers
  setup       Setup the complete MCP platform
  status      Show platform status
  team        Manage internal platform teams
  update      Update installed platform services to a release

Flags:
      --debug     Enable debug mode with structured error logging
  -h, --help      help for mcp-runtime
  -v, --version   version for mcp-runtime

Use "mcp-runtime [command] --help" for more information about a command.
